            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Chay Làng Ta",
            "review_text": "Ny\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam3 contributions\n0\nGreat\nJun 2026 • Family\nI just experienced the \"Lang Ta\" vegetarian restaurant at 179 Ly Chinh Thang and was truly impressed. As soon as I stepped inside, I felt the incredibly tranquil, cozy, and rustic atmosphere, just like its name \"Lang Ta\" (Our Village). Finding such a peaceful corner to enjoy breakfast in the bustling District 3 is absolutely wonderful. As for the food, it deserves a 10/10 for quality. The menu is incredibly diverse, and the dishes are very unique: The appetizers include the refreshing three-flavor spring rolls and the fragrant sugarcane skewers wrapped in rice noodles – very appetizing. The side dishes, like the savory stir-fried chicken thighs, are very appetizing and go well with rice, while the three-flavor fried rice has fluffy, delicious grains and isn't greasy at all. Especially, the restaurant has excellent hot pot options. Those who like a rich, spicy and sour flavor should try the tom yum broth, while those who love a rich, creamy, and fragrant broth should try the hot pot here – the broth is naturally sweet from the vegetables and not at all harsh. The staff were very lovely, gentle, and attentive. The prices were absolutely worth the quality of the food and the ambiance. I will definitely come back often and bring my whole family along. A truly worthwhile vegetarian dining experience for those who appreciate tranquility and healthy eating!\nRead more\nWritten June 20, 2026\nNhà hàng chay Làng Ta\nThank you for your trust and for sharing your beautiful experience at Làng Ta. We wish you good health, happiness, and peace always.\nWritten June 22, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
